<title>RUSSIA: Yeltsin says to settle Caspian problems on return.</title>
<headline>Yeltsin says to settle Caspian problems on return.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Boris Yeltsin agreed on Saturday with his Kazakh counterpart to resolve differences on the division of the Caspian Sea's oil and gas reserves when the Russian leader returns to work after convalescing from surgery.</p>
<p>Presidential spokesman Sergei Yastrzhembsky told a news briefing after Yeltsin met Kazakh President Nursultan Nazarbayev at the Barvikha sanatorium outside Moscow: &quot;They agreed they will settle all the key questions when President Yeltsin finally returns to his office in the Kremlin.&quot;</p>
<p>Yeltsin's doctor said on Friday the president's convalescence from his November 5 heart bypass operation would end around December 20, although he might make trips to the Kremlin before then.</p>
<p>He will spend the next two to three weeks at Barvikha.</p>
<p>--Moscow newsroom +7 095 941 8520</p>
